{"title":"Lattice Payments","sub":"A bank wants a fintech. Is it worth the premium?","type":"M&A","industry":"Banking","geo":"United Kingdom","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"M&A · premium vs synergies · build, partner or buy","prompt":"A large UK bank wants to offer its small-business customers a modern payments app. Lattice, a fast-growing fintech, has agreed in principle to sell for $180M. The bank's strategy head asks you whether the price makes sense.","clarify":[{"q":"Lattice's numbers?","a":"EBITDA of $6M, growing fast. Similar fintechs trade at about 15× EBITDA."},{"q":"The bank's plan?","a":"Offer the app to its 2 million small-business customers. Pilots suggest about 3% would adopt, each earning about $100 of profit a year."},{"q":"Cost savings?","a":"About $1M a year from shared compliance and hosting."},{"q":"Integration?","a":"About $10M one-off. Lattice's founders have said they may leave after a year."},{"q":"How to value synergies?","a":"Use 10× the yearly synergy, a little below Lattice's multiple because they are less certain."}],"structure":{"root":"Should the bank buy Lattice for $180M?","branches":[{"head":"Standalone value","items":["EBITDA × multiple"]},{"head":"Premium paid","items":["Price − standalone value"]},{"head":"Synergies","items":["Cross-selling to the bank's customers","Cost savings","Minus integration"]},{"head":"Alternatives","items":["Partner or white-label","Build"]}]},"hypothesis":"Paying $180M for a company worth about $90M on its own means paying a $90M premium for synergies. I'd check whether the cross-selling can realistically earn that back.","questions":[{"q":"What is the bank paying for, beyond Lattice itself?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Standalone value: $6M × 15 = <b>$90M</b>. The premium for synergies is <b>$90M</b>.</p> <p>To justify it at 10×, the bank needs about <b>$9M a year</b> of synergies, plus enough to cover $10M of integration.</p>"},{"q":"Can the synergies deliver that?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"399.26pt\" height=\"176.64pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 399.26 176.64\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 176.64 L 399.26 176.64 L 399.26 0 L 0 0 L 0 176.64 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 46.1 139.04 L 392.06 139.04 L 392.06 11.528 L 46.1 11.528 L 46.1 139.04 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"94.931675\" y=\"139.04\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(60.105893 155.265) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-30\" d=\"M 1850 -77 Q 1312 -77 925 131 Q 538 339 269 704 L 666 1037 Q 902 723 1190 560 Q 1478 397 1869 397 Q 2349 397 2601 627 Q 2854 858 2854 1242 Q 2854 1453 2771 1600 Q 2688 1747 2505 1846 Q 2323 1946 2029 2010 L 1664 2093 Q 1261 2189 979 2342 Q 698 2496 550 2739 Q 403 2982 403 3322 Q 403 3718 588 3990 Q 774 4262 1110 4403 Q 1446 4544 1882 4544 Q 2387 4544 2748 4358 Q 3110 4173 3360 3814 L 2957 3520 Q 2778 3776 2512 3923 Q 2246 4070 1856 4070 Q 1427 4070 1180 3884 Q 934 3699 934 3341 Q 934 3130 1027 2989 Q 1120 2848 1305 2755 Q 1491 2662 1773 2598 L 2138 2515 Q 2573 2419 2848 2252 Q 3123 2086 3254 1843 Q 3386 1600 3386 1267 Q 3386 858 3200 557 Q 3014 256 2672 89 Q 2330 -77 1850 -77 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" d=\"M 1914 0 L 1274 0 Q 1011 0 870 153 Q 730 307 730 544 L 730 2854 L 186 2854 L 186 3302 L 493 3302 Q 659 3302 720 3369 Q 781 3437 781 3603 L 781 4218 L 1242 4218 L 1242 3302 L 1965 3302 L 1965 2854 L 1242 285