PlexSans-Regular-40\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(253.262775 35.64) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(336.028325 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" d=\"M 1920 -77 Q 1414 -77 1068 92 Q 723 262 547 556 Q 371 851 371 1216 Q 371 1670 620 1942 Q 870 2214 1274 2323 L 1274 2374 Q 922 2496 714 2768 Q 506 3040 506 3424 Q 506 3936 880 4240 Q 1254 4544 1920 4544 Q 2586 4544 2960 4240 Q 3334 3936 3334 3424 Q 3334 3040 3126 2768 Q 2918 2496 2566 2374 L 2566 2323 Q 2970 2214 3219 1942 Q 3469 1670 3469 1216 Q 3469 851 3293 556 Q 3117 262 2774 92 Q 2432 -77 1920 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2387 390 2643 601 Q 2899 813 2899 1190 L 2899 1325 Q 2899 1702 2643 1913 Q 2387 2125 1920 2125 Q 1453 2125 1197 1913 Q 941 1702 941 1325 L 941 1190 Q 941 813 1197 601 Q 1453 390 1920 390 z\nM 1920 2573 Q 2336 2573 2557 2755 Q 2778 2938 2778 3277 L 2778 3373 Q 2778 3712 2557 3894 Q 2336 4077 1920 4077 Q 1504 4077 1283 3894 Q 1062 3712 1062 3373 L 1062 3277 Q 1062 2938 1283 2755 Q 1504 2573 1920 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pd2fb3de91e\"><rect x=\"46.1\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Price vs value ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Cross-selling: 2 million × 3% = 60k users × $100 = <b>$6M a year</b>. Cost savings: $1M. Total $7M a year, worth $70M.</p> <p>Maximum sensible price: $90M + $70M − $10M = <b>$150M</b>, $30M below the agreed price.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> at $180M the bank would pay away more than all the value it creates, even if the 3% adoption is achieved.</p>"},{"q":"What alternatives would you put to the bank?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Partner (white-label):</b> offer Lattice's app under the bank's brand and share revenue. If the bank keeps about 70% of the cross-sell profit, it earns ~$4.2M a year with no premium and no integration</li> <li><b>Renegotiate:</b> offer up to ~$150M, with part paid only if adoption passes 3%</li> <li><b>Build:</b> slower and risky for a bank; only if the app is truly strategic</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Don't buy Lattice at $180M. Lattice is worth about $90M on its own, and realistic synergies (about $7M a year from cross-selling and cost savings) justify at most about $150M. I recommend a white-label partnership, which gives the bank's customers the app and earns most of the cross-sell profit without paying a premium; or a revised offer of up to $150M with an earn-out. Risk: a rival bank may buy Lattice instead. Next step: test adoption with 20,000 customers through a partnership pilot.","great":["Calculates the premium paid for synergies","Turns the premium into the synergies needed per year","Shows the deal destroys value even if the plan works","Offers partnership and renegotiation as alternatives"],"id":64,"slug":"lattice-payments"}